WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.460
2017 was the year the 
Anime industry went into overdrive.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.460
I mean, I hope I'm not the only one who feels this.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.420
You have the big boys just fucking 
pouring in money trying to get a piece of that pie.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.300
More anime coming out than 
any of us could ever conceivably watch,

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.700
and the medium itself starting to 
break out to the mainstream consensus.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:20.880
In terms of the actual anime that came out, 
however, I'd say, overall,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.740
it was OK.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.660
We have the usual standouts in
 Action, Slice of Life, and Romance.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.520
Isekai shows no sign of slowing down,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.080
to the point where a piece of my soul 
gets transported to another world

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.640
every time have I to say, "transported to another world."

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.579
[applause in the background]
But we're getting to see the 
revival of traditional fantasy again!

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:36.820
[applause in the background]
Who would have thought?

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.540
Mecha fans, though, unfortunately, 
once again were left in the dust.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.880
I'm sorry, mecha fans!

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.760
2018 is gonna be your year, I swear to God!

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.380
But I think what was really missing this year

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.720
was that new big breakout hit
to really capture the community.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.120
Alright, enough bullshit.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.860
Crunchyroll are, once again, 
hosting the Anime Awards and

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.940
well, I know our memories are still fresh
about what happened last year.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.940
But they've had time to listen to...

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:01.274
[arguing in the background]
The small amount of criticism that they got,

00:01:01.274 --> 00:01:03.059
and have an entirely new award system.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.320
It's not perfect, but just looking at the nominations,
it's already a hell of a lot better.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:08.720
Your votes still matter,

00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:13.960
but judges hold equal power over the outcome, 
to avoid this being the 'Yuri!!! on Ice' season 2 Awards.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.820
They've asked me to give my opinions of
the best things to come out of Anime in 2017.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:18.960
For full disclosure:

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.850
I am not being paid to make this video,

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.030
but they are flying me out to the event
cause it's gonna be a live show this year,

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.680
which should be very interesting.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.300
And, without further ado, here we go.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:34.860
It's no secret that CG and Anime
have not had the best relationship.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.620
For years, it's like the two have been put into
an arranged marriage that neither side wants to be in.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.040
For every small step forward 
Polygon Pictures took with their work,

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.260
we got a 'Berserk (2017)';

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:48.800
taking us so many steps back,
we moonwalked back to the Jurassic Era.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.810
And the best we could ever hope for
was something like all 10 episodes-

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.320
Yes, count them, *10* episodes of
'KADO: The Right Answer'

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.140
That could give us a story interesting
enough that we could look past the CG.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:01.860
For me, though, the worst thing
is a show like 'Inuyashiki',

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.940
where the CG is not bad,
but it's the constant switching from

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:08.300
2D to 3D to 2D to 3D to 2D again,

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.200
oh, no, wait we're 3D again to

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.320
God, just make up your fucking mind already!

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.680
Being incredibly jarring in any scene
that just makes you want to scream:

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.180
"Jesus Christ, just get a divorce already!"

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:24.180
"It is painful to see you two
try to force this and make it work!"

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:27.120
But this year, 'Land of the Lustrous'
came along and told us:

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:43.560
♪ Land of the Lustrous OST - Phosphophyllite ♪

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.660
"You know what?"

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:48.060
"Maybe all those years of marriage counseling
finally did you some good."

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.100
[ ORA ORA ORA ]

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.060
Action is judged by the quality of their action scenes.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.600
Which, in Anime, of course, is dominated by

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.560
[echoed yelling]
the good old Anime fight scenes!

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.120
Which, you know, I'm a bit of fan of.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.480
And 2017 was no exception.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.480
'Boruto' came out carrying Naruto's torch

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:08.360
of putting all your year's resources
into one amazing fight.

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:10.620
'Fate/Apocrypha' had some fantastic looking fights, but

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:13.820
God damn, do I not give a shit about this series

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.940
or any of the characters involved
to let these fights have an impact.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.600
And even Kyoto Animation were flexing for the hell of it with these one or two little moments.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.520
They were just like:

00:03:21.549 --> 00:03:22.960
"Hey, that's a cool fight scene."

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.780
"I mean, we're just here making a cute little moe show,
so there's nothing we can do to really compet-"

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.560
[INTENSE GRUNTING NOISES]

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.060
[clearing throat]

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.680
"Sorry, don-don't know what came over me there, but uh"

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.120
"nice, nice fight scenes."

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:35.300
"They're cute."

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.140
In terms of singular big fights, though,

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.540
factoring in overall build up, writing,
execution, and animation

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:44.620
'My Hero Academia' just took the piss,
competing against itself for the top spot

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.200
with Deku vs. Todoroki
and Stain vs. the U.A. Alliance.

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.020
Then, somewhere over here

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:55.920
is Eren vs. the Armored Titan for its fantastic technical choreography of a Grappler vs. Striker fight.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:58.700
I'll also put Kiss-Shot vs. Araragi
somewhere in the middle

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:01.920
for its technical prowess, and
just how fucking fun and ridiculous it was.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.580
Now, for those wondering where Goku vs. Jiren is:

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:09.140
I haven't actually been watching 'Dragon Ball Super', nor do I feel like marathoning a hundred episodes right now,

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.620
and for a fight of that magnitude
I'm not just gonna watch it out of context,

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.820
but from the reaction I've seen,
 it'll be a contender for the top spot.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:21.440
That being said, in terms of overall action the show that most consistently put the biggest smile on my face was

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.760
'Re:CREATORS'

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.560
Which isn't even a nomination, by the way.

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:27.440
Now, how can I be arguing this over other contenders,

00:04:27.449 --> 00:04:30.089
which are probably, technically, better executed?

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:31.360
Well, you know what?

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:33.220
As great as everything else was

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:35.310
I've seen Yutaka Nakamura cuts,

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:37.980
I've seen brilliantly choreographed fights,

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:42.510
I've seen well written and well built-up 
stories concluded with fists.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.440
Do you know what I haven't seen?

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:47.020
Fucking magical girl versus fantasy knight.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:49.529
'JoJo's' characters versus visual novel villains.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.240
Harem love interest getting powered up and
combating fighting game characters.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:57.720
A small mech with a big mech versus small mechs with big mechs and a small little girl an-

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.660
What is even happening?!

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.520
These scenes were the rule of cool on steroids.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:06.700
It's a full-on wet dream for anyone 
who likes meta media, and is a fan of Anime.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.980
It's not perfect, it's not completely polished,

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:12.900
but God damn is it so much fucking fun.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:16.329
Rei Hiroe is a bloody madman for writing this concept,

00:05:16.329 --> 00:05:18.120
and I salute him for it.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.600
[old film projector noise]

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.600
In recent times, Anime films have had
a different treatment internationally.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:26.860
Before, no matter how excited you were for a film,
there'd be no way for you to watch it,

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:30.680
unless you invested years of your life learning
Japanese and had a fresh plane ticket to Japan.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.780
Or, alternatively you could've watched cam-rips,

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:36.060
which, I'm sure none of you did
because we're not fucking savages.

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:40.160
In contrast, 2017 was the year
we could start seeing Anime films regularly.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.740
Largely thanks to licensing companies being on the ball,

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.720
with international releases quicker
than we've ever seen before.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:48.840
If a film was announced there was
actually a chance you'd see some screenings

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:51.480
if you live near a populated area, which was amazing!

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.040
Even though America with their
'Your Name.' release was more like

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:58.360
[from the other side of the room]
Well...

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.820
[from the other side of the room]
Well, at least we got there eventually.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:03.340
But thanks to that, 'Your Name.'
is up for nomination for Best Film this year.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:08.350
So of course there was only ever gonna be one pick
for my favorite Anime film to get an American release:

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:11.280
'Sword Art Online: Ordinal Scale'

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:15.280
[holding back laughter]

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:20.740
[bad flute sounds]

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:22.560
Music in Anime is important to me -

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:23.760
if you didn't already know -

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.580
but there weren't many shows I watched this year

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.560
that actively made me want to go back
and listen to the tracks, over and over again.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:33.900
'Re:CREATORS' continued Hiroyuki Sawano's legacy of composing the same five awesome songs

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:38.400
in his latest attempt to induce pure, unadulterated soundgasms by blowing off your eardrums,

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:39.880
and I still fucking love it.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:43.779
I mean, I went into this show completely blind and when I first heard the tracks my first thought was jokingly:

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.300
[yelling]
AYE AYE, IT'S JUST A BIT LOUD ISN'T IT?

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:48.940
[yelling]
YEAH YEAH, I-I-I-IT'S JUST A TAD LOUD

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.380
Do you think, by chance,
we're about to hear a Sawano drop?

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:52.180
Hahah

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.180
Ahahaha

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:53.680
Uh-

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.140
[Sawano drop]

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:56.300
Wait, are you fucking kiddi-

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:59.600
[really loud]
♪ Re:CREATORS OST - Layers ♪

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.720
But, to me, there were only
two clear contenders for the top spot,

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:04.800
and they were both Fantasy shows.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.500
'Magus' Bride' consistently had pieces that would leave 
you in awe of the natural beauty of the world it was in.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:12.600
They'd fit right in with something like
the documentary 'Planet Earth,'

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:15.840
that makes you just want to sit back
and reflect on Nature's beauty,

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:19.540
while setting the tone of this magical, fantastical place.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:23.360
And I think with all tracks considered,
it has the strongest OST, overall.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:27.060
But in terms of individual tracks
that blew me away, I have to go with

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.059
Kevin Penkin's work on 'Made in Abyss.'

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:32.520
I mean, I've already used this drop
so many fucking times already,

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:33.140
but fuck you!

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:35.440
This is my video, and I want to hear it again.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:41.460
♪ Made in Abyss OST - Hanezeve Caradhina ♪

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:44.960
I could be mowing the lawn, washing the dishes,
or doing anything else,

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:50.080
but if I hear these tracks time stops, and it just immediately transports me to another world.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:50.880
Oh, no, wait-

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:51.960
Fuck. Fuck! FUCK!

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:54.320
Huge credit to Kevin Penkin for composing it all.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:58.080
Who, surprisingly enough by his name, is not Japanese!

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.340
Who could've known?

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:01.560
Yes, he's actually an Australian bloke,

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:05.360
though, there's absolutely no way
you'd be able to tell that just by talking to him.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:12.700
♪ "I come from a land down under" ♪
♪ Men At Work - Down Under ♪

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:15.580
When I first watched 'Made in Abyss,'
I wasn't looking forward to it.

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:17.500
I took one look at the poster and thought:

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.560
"Man, I don't wanna watch another stupid-ass 
loli-adventure-slice of life-nothing show."

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:26.020
But as soon as that first big song hit,
I was absolutely blown away.

00:08:26.220 --> 00:08:29.820
I marveled at the beauty and scale
of the journey I was about to undertake

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:32.200
that enveloped me into this new world.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.480
I was ready to explore.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:34.640
I was ready to feel.

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:39.140
And just with one track,
it had sold me on the entire series.

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:40.940
[instruments stop playing]

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:48.540
Last year, 'Rakugo' was the underground
breakout hit, that all the critics were praising as

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:52.240
the one, amazing, overlooked, Drama masterpiece.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:55.560
With 'March comes in like a lion' 
and 'Fune wo Amu' left in the back like:

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.680
[from the back of the room]
Hey, you know, we were-

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.180
[from the back of the room]
we were pretty good, too.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:01.423
This year, 'Rakugo' came back in full force

00:09:01.423 --> 00:09:04.680
as the auteur pick of the Anime
that really gave us the masterclass of

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:08.260
a beautifully written, delicately crafted Drama series.

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.300
And, once again,

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.840
'March comes in like a lion' season 2
was there in the back like:

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:14.740
[from the back of the room]
Yeah, you know, still-

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:16.300
[from the back of the room]
still pretty good, too.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:17.940
And as much as I'm joking about this,

00:09:17.950 --> 00:09:22.060
I'm one of the people who never got back to it,
despite thinking it had an amazing first episode

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:26.140
and hearing from a few people, who did watch it,
that it was, indeed, amazing.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:29.360
So, with that in mind,
I don't think I'm fully equipped to judge this category,

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:31.660
as I feel like it's a contest between these two shows.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:35.007
Since, as great as the drama in 
'Made in Abyss' and 'Magus' Bride' was,

00:09:35.007 --> 00:09:36.920
their strength lies in other places, too.

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:39.360
And the award really needed
its own Fantasy Genre Award,

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:41.380
so that these two shows can duke it out

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.660
over the corpse of every Isekai show
that have come out in the past few years.

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:48.320
[laugh track]

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.220
I don't usually like Anime Comedies.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:53.560
It's hard for me to find a show
that doesn't rely too heavily on Anime slapstick,

00:09:53.560 --> 00:09:56.260
or that one joke
being beaten over our heads, continually.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:00.200
And, any that I do like usually are only
able to get a small chuckle out of me, at most.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.550
So, I normally look over Comedy Anime
compared to other genres

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:08.440
But, despite that, I found the show this year that continually had me rolling around laughing.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:11.120
Every episode had something new,
it did not overstay its welcome,

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:15.320
and it was an experience 
I could not stop laughing at, for one reason or another.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.440
And that show was:

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:19.540
'KonoSuba' Season-

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:21.200
'Neo Yokio.'

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:23.380
I am not joking.

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.340
["sexy" music playing while
Gigguk slowly says "sakuga"]

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:30.760
When talking about animation, it's very easy
to focus entirely on Action and Fight scenes,

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:32.220
which we've already covered.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:33.793
So, I wanted to take this time to talk about

00:10:33.793 --> 00:10:36.080
some miscellaneous things that've
just stood out to me visually,

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:39.660
like 'Land of the Lustrous's'
amazingly dynamic fight scenes!

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:42.480
Which, were not actually my favorite shots in this show,

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:46.640
as that belongs to this long shot of Diamond - this girl - trying to hide from a monster.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:51.420
I love the way the camera follows her around to build that tension, and really get you into her shoes

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.520
giving that sense of claustrophobia.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:56.900
And a shot like this is something
that fully takes advantage of doing a 3D Anime,

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:58.900
which, *mmph* brilliant cinematography.

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.900
Okay, not so much animation,
but speaking of not-animation

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:04.580
the Ghibli inspired landscapes in 
'Made in Abyss' were just

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.200
*mwah*

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:06.740
absolutely breathtaking.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:09.800
I could stare at panning shots of these landscapes
all fucking day long,

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:12.900
cause these were the sexiest things
to come out of 2017.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:16.040
"Draw me like you draw one of your
'Made in Abyss' backgrounds."

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:17.700
[furious breathing]
"Oh yeah"

00:11:17.700 --> 00:11:20.840
For real though, my favorite animation this year
came out of 'A Silent Voice',

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.620
specifically for the character animation.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:26.400
Yes, I know It's unfair to compare
movie animation to TV series,

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:27.660
but tell that to the judges.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:32.640
To express emotion without any words is a hard enough skill for professional actors to convey in live-action,

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:38.340
so it blows my mind how Kyoto Animation
were able to do it so well with a fucking drawing.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.020
Which is something we don't see so often

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:43.680
in a medium that has no problem expressing itself through dialogue and exposition.

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:47.800
['Fate/Apocrypha' characters all talking over each other]

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.000
Gigguk: "Can you repeat that please?
I'm not quite getting it."

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:55.619
In contrast, this girl says more saying nothing than 90% of Anime characters who can talk all fucking day long,

00:11:55.649 --> 00:11:58.380
through the nuance of
her facial expression and body language.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:03.380
Never before have I seen so many complex emotions,
so subtly conveyed in a look, or an action.

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:07.120
And, all I can say is I feel no one could have
tackled this better than Kyoto Animation.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:13.020
Who, for all these years, were just training - levelling up, so now they have reached their absolute final form of:

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.480
Cute Girl Animation.

00:12:14.640 --> 00:12:16.200
But, if I can't go with movies,

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:18.240
even though I could never get into
'Little Witch Academia,'

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:21.160
even I have to admit how
breathtaking some of the cuts were.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:23.740
If 'Magus' Bride' was able to give a magical atmosphere,

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:26.140
'Little Witch' was magic in motion.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.720
Now, if only there was something more
I could actually latch on to-

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:31.180
♪ Gurren Laggan OP - Sorairo Days in the background ♪
Ohohohoho! Wait! Wait! Shit!

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.480
♪ Gurren Laggan OP - Sorairo Days in the background ♪
Are they doing the reference I think they're doing?!

00:12:37.460 --> 00:12:39.560
Slice of Life feels like a bit of a cluttered category,

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:42.540
as it looks like the Awards have combined
Slice of Life and Romance,

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.420
so I'm just gonna split these up myself.

00:12:44.540 --> 00:12:46.280
Slice of Life was an easy decision for me,

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:49.280
because aside from what I'm sure
is most people's pick being in Comedy,

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:53.040
'Girls' Last Tour' was a show about
cute girls doing cute things,

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:55.320
and I actually liked it.

00:12:55.520 --> 00:13:00.020
Yes, that's right. Cute moe girls have finally broken down Garnt "Motherfucking Tea" Gigguk

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:01.420
And I'm not sure exactly why.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:05.480
But, the juxtaposition of cute girls exploring
a desolate, bleak, post-apocalyptic world

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.980
with such an innocent charm,
sprinkled in with some life philosophy,

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:10.380
created this atmosphere that was the perfect balance

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.740
of light-hearted goodness
and thought-provoking moments.

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:15.480
Romance, on the other hand,
had some very strong contenders.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:19.679
I loved 'MMO Junkie's' take at
relationships formed via online interactions,

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:22.340
even if it did end up becoming
'Coincidences: The Anime.'

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:25.460
And I really, really enjoyed the comedic look
at different couples in

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:29.140
[trying to say 'Tsuredure Children' and failing]

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:30.180
[wheeze laugh while hitting the desk]

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:32.880
FUCK! I can never pronounce the fucking name!

00:13:32.880 --> 00:13:36.880
so much so, that if I can't put 'Neo Yokio,'
this can also be my pick for Comedy.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:40.350
But, for Romance,
the show I want to talk about is "Tsuki ga Kirei.'

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:43.769
It's rare to be able to find a Romance series
that feels so grounded.

00:13:43.770 --> 00:13:47.740
It's a series that explores teenage relationships
in a way you don't normally see in Anime.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:52.600
For one, the characters in this Anime don't particularly feel like Anime characters, in the typical sense.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.920
Nothing is overdramatised, nothing is overplayed,

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:57.100
it just feels real.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:00.630
If you're looking for a show that portrays
the innocence of genuine teenage romance,

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.220
this is your show.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:05.010
But that's all I want to say, as I don't really care
too much about every other category,

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.010
so let's just get to The Big Boy Award.

00:14:11.670 --> 00:14:13.660
This is it, the Big One.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:15.120
And this was a tough decision.

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:16.400
I mean, on one hand,

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:21.300
I had my shounen-trash side loving just how much 'HeroAca' is bringing the genre back to its roots,

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:23.760
or 'Made in Abyss' completely blowing me away,

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:26.100
or 'Rakugo's' beautifully crafted series.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:29.220
Hell, I only talked about the phenomenal CG
in 'Land of the Lustrous,'

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:31.320
but it was just a great show all around.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:35.800
And, God, I'm pretty sure I'm the only one who had
as much fun with 'Re:CREATORS' as I did,

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:37.080
despite everything.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.380
But, there can only be one winner,

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:45.340
which is why, my pick for
Anime of the Year 2017 goes to:

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.660
♪ "You'll never see it coming" ♪
♪ Persona 5 OST - Last Surprise ♪

00:14:47.660 --> 00:14:52.780
♪ Persona 5 OST - Last Surprise ♪
Persona 5, for being the best Anime I played all yea-

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:53.760
It's 'Made in Abyss.'

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.200
'Made in A'byss' was my favorite Anime this year.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:15:02.800
♪ Persona 5 OST - Life Will Change  ♪

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:07.460
Voting is now open for the Awards at theanimeawards.com for some of the categories,

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.760
so you can go there to vote, or check out the nominees.

00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:14.680
I trust you all to make the right decision,
and not to be swayed by my opinions at all.

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.460
[whispering very soflty]
When Best Action is open,

00:15:16.460 --> 00:15:18.900
[whispering very soflty]
you can put a write-in vote for 'Re:CREATORS.'

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:21.360
But aside from that, thank you very much to:

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:28.080
[reading out Patreon supporters]

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:32.460
and everyone else on Patreon for helping to support me for this month, and making this video possible

00:15:32.580 --> 00:15:37.060
I'm really hoping I could say goodbye
to 2017 Anime now, and start completely fresh,

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:39.520
so until then, quick outro today:

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:43.060
I've been Gigguk, and I will see you all next time.

